#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059496 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64edd709-3f6c-59e1-ae1f-bca25eca0483" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection of a Sine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "e03cba93-339e-578e-aae8-55c98669c2ff" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-4646" :question/problem "The graph above represents a transformed sine curve. What is the equation of the graph?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/89614702470515495bff6e9a7d2ee710.png)" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/da96b4325b5cb99127a208386e5d33a5.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\sin x$.\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\sin x$.\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $8$ to give $y=-8\\sin x$.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-8\\sin x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059497 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85090bdf-4f1b-5f79-a751-48521ad98895" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection of a Sine or Cosine Curve Over the Vertical Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "4f63d3b6-1c1e-5cc3-8fe8-6f580a298c90" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-4647" :question/problem "The graph above shows the function $y=2\\sin(kx)$. What is the value of $k$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/643d638672fe9059c6151e7469aa87c1.png)" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/eb76dc56d2a6336bf24e289a588ed2db.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\sin x$.\n- Then, reflect it across the $y$-axis.\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $2$.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of\n\n$$\ny=2\\sin(-x)\n$$\n\nHence, $k=-1$.\n\nNotice that, because the sine function is odd, the $y$-axis reflection has the same effect as the $x$-axis reflection, i.e.,\n\n$$\n2\\sin(-x) = -2\\sin x\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=-2\\sin x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059498 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fe335eb-dc4a-5ea0-83cf-ad929e19b908" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection and Shifting of a Sine or Cosine Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "cbf9d044-3541-51fb-8131-3911909d334b" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-4648" :question/problem "The graph above represents a transformed cosine curve. What is the equation of the graph?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/8aaec5b66acc1171f90f49727710df5e.png)" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/7f231c9d8d6e80fb1a38e120cf2a63bc.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\cos x$.\n- Finally, translate it by $2$ units **up** to give $y=-\\cos x+2$.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of\n\n$$\ny=-\\cos x+2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059499 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f71a8f16-93d4-5e5a-9b8b-e29efc682430" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection of a Cosine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "3e380a56-e9aa-58d6-8584-2da67a66bd02" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-4650" :question/problem "The graph above represents a transformed cosine curve. What is the equation of the graph?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/2a0825f8193233d0c8cb3a5362970095.png)" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/259/Source/Images/3be3200eb0bc3d37ac7b7b8e68404259.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\cos x$.\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $6$ to give $y=-6\\cos x$.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-6\\cos x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64edd709-3f6c-59e1-ae1f-bca25eca0483" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection of a Sine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a83db9b-df8e-5aa3-8382-967010f123e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{4}-sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246300} {:answer/id #uuid "abb26962-a17c-533e-be05-7f0b9110cfa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡(x+\\frac{7}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246301} {:answer/id #uuid "e39ca93a-b5ad-59d1-ba78-65dedd7ca39c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{7}{4}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246302} {:answer/id #uuid "0ca59985-a961-5ce0-a8c6-c8e420308b50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡(\\frac{7x}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246303} {:answer/id #uuid "ad836414-87ed-5eb3-a42f-6d20cfaf7cf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡x-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e39ca93a-b5ad-59d1-ba78-65dedd7ca39c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{7}{4}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246302} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4a6131d-15df-5c9d-8dcd-cd7408ac679f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246299}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e7f3919-6ad5-5ead-b766-27f8f2a6a127" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-118348" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/f2d3945780d6d042ae5fa01905cf7740fca0f5f80307124556a1b4724f691683.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/6ba976f250811d1ba3109f4aecbfdb2a4de4ee86300fa867e80e2087aa21601f.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-sin⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{7}{4}$ to give $y=-\\frac{7}{4}sin⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\frac{7}{4}sin⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64edd709-3f6c-59e1-ae1f-bca25eca0483" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection of a Sine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0d964d1-58a7-5097-a9a5-1c5c360da628" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡(\\frac{x}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246307} {:answer/id #uuid "1a926244-3d85-5fe1-853c-c778b0716dcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{4}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246308} {:answer/id #uuid "5ab7ae0d-0c16-5d81-ad6e-42fd13eb50b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡x-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246309} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ad43bd-4400-5c83-8426-693c339b8ee0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡(x-\\frac{1}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246310} {:answer/id #uuid "e032ae98-cb80-52b2-92c5-7494b088d8be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}-sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a926244-3d85-5fe1-853c-c778b0716dcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{4}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246308} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1064623-4796-5756-8444-8d3806df5971" :answe